name: Planning aliases preserve prerequisites, scope limits and explicit action choice
size: 120x36
cwd: @TMP_TARGET
env-unset: ANTHROPIC_API_KEY OPENAI_API_KEY KUZUSHI_MODEL KUZUSHI_LANGGRAPH_BRIDGE NODE_OPTIONS NO_COLOR KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/taint_planning.py @TMP_TARGET @ART prepare
require-wrapper-flow:
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 READY THE MAP RUN | ready
submit: setg ui.auto_open_activity false
submit: use taint-iris-next
submit: run .
submit: logs
require-live-snap: 20 Choose an exact tool | explicit-action-required
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/taint_planning.py @TMP_TARGET @ART before
ask: Does selecting a module avoid launching its experimental primary or substituting a different scan or model action?
paste-file: @ART/plan-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 needs usable Kuzushi context | plan-prerequisite
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/taint_planning.py @TMP_TARGET @ART plan
paste-file: @ART/alias-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 25 Missing context or source inventory | alias-prerequisite
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/taint_planning.py @TMP_TARGET @ART alias
paste-file: @ART/replay-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Outcome · failed | recorded-prerequisite
ask: Are the missing inventory/context and recovery guidance honest, with no finding or completed Scan claimed by either alias?
resize: 160x48
live-snap: prerequisite-160x48
resize: 96x89
live-snap: prerequisite-96x89
resize: 80x24
live-snap: prerequisite-80x24
resize: 60x20
live-snap: prerequisite-60x20
resize: 40x12
require-live-snap: 20 Outcome · failed | prerequisite-40x12
expect: Missing context or
expect: source inventory
keys: NPage NPage
live-snap: prerequisite-detail-40x12
ask: Are failed outcome, limitations and recovery controls readable through paging at each size?
resize: 120x36
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-quit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
env: HOME=@TMP_HOME KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 NO_COLOR=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
require-live-snap: 30 READY THE MAP RUN | restarted-setup
paste-file: @ART/replay-command.txt
keys: Enter
require-live-snap: 20 Outcome · failed | recovered-prerequisite
require-shell: python3 -B @REPO/scripts/devex/fixtures/taint_planning.py @TMP_TARGET @ART restart
ask: Does no-color restart retain both prerequisite receipts and the earlier result bytes without creating work or leaving fresh Setup?
keys: C-c
require-live-snap: 10 CONFIRM SESSION EXIT | explicit-restart-quit
keys: y
require-exit: 10
